  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Anticipatory Action for food security and livelihoods protection of farmers and fisherfolks during flood in Mindanao and typhoon in the Philippines` Eastern Seaboard</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of this Anticipatory Action project is to mitigate, and to a certain extent, prevent the impact of flooding and typhoon on people&apos;s lives, livelihoods, and assets. It also seeks to build the resilience of poor and vulnerable farmers and fisherfolks by providing them with capacities and resources that will enable them to prepare prior to the onset or peak of a hazard. The specific Anticipatory Action interventions are early warning/agro-climatic messages and provision of multi-purpose cash assistance worth Php 3,250 or USD 56. The project will benefit 5,519 beneficiaries in Surigao del Norte (typhoon) and Cotabato (flooding).</narrative>
  </description>
